@startuml dataflow_example_drop_dim_3d
' Worked example: two variables on a 3x3x3 grid, the second varying along
' two of the three dimensions. Every number here is from an actual run.
' Grids: one panel per x0 (= stratum), rows x1, columns x2, index space.
' Render: plantuml docs/dataflow_example_drop_dim_3d.puml

title Example 4 -- a variable that drops one of three dimensions

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "call" {
  :GenerateData(num_obs=12, num_dims=3, ratio_dims=1,
                density=12/27, seed=1,
                num_vars=2, var_dims=[3, 2], overlap=0.5)
  .generate(...);
}

partition "validate and configure" {
  :shape = [3, 3, 3], 27 sites, density_zero = 3/27 = 0.111;

  :<b>MultiVarDimensionsConfig</b>
  stream(1, VAR_DIMS, 1) picks which 2 dims var1 varies along
  -> var1 varies along x0, x1 and is constant along x2;

  :<b>MultiVarSparsityConfig</b>: densities are shares of each
  variable's own grid
  var0: 12/27 of 27 = 12
  var1: 12/27 of 9 (x0 * x1) = 4
  <b>dim_split = 0</b>: every variable varies along x0;
}

partition "placement of var0" {
  :<b>LHS stage</b>, stream(1, LHS), n_s = 3
    x0 = 0, 1, 2
    x1 = 2, 1, 0
    x2 = 0, 2, 1
  -> sites (0,2,0), (1,1,2), (2,0,1);
  note right
    after the LHS stage (L = LHS site, . = vacant)
           x0=0         x0=1         x0=2
           x2: 0 1 2    x2: 0 1 2    x2: 0 1 2
      x1=0     . . .        . . .        . L .
      x1=1     . . .        . . L        . . .
      x1=2     L . .        . . .        . . .
    One site per stratum, and each coordinate of
    each of the three axes used once.
  end note

  :<b>fill</b>: 12 - 3 = 9 points, 8 free cells per stratum
  -> 3 per stratum, from stream(1, STRATUM, j);
  note right
    var0 placed (f = fill site)
           x0=0         x0=1         x0=2
           x2: 0 1 2    x2: 0 1 2    x2: 0 1 2
      x1=0     . f f        f f .        . L .
      x1=1     . . .        . . L        f . .
      x1=2     L f .        . . f        . f f
  end note
}

partition "placement of var1: overlap through the projection" {
  :<b>pinned coordinate</b>: stream(1, CONST_COORD, 1, 2)
  -> var1 sits at <b>x2 = 1</b>;

  :<b>proj_j(S0)</b>: var0's sites in stratum j seen through
  var1's dims, i.e. x2 dropped
    stratum 0: x1 = 0, 2      p_0 = 2
    stratum 1: x1 = 0, 1, 2   p_1 = 3
    stratum 2: x1 = 0, 1, 2   p_2 = 3;
  note right
    var1's own plane (x0, x1)
    (P = some var0 site along x2)
            x1=0 x1=1 x1=2
      x0=0   P    .    P
      x0=1   P    P    P
      x0=2   P    P    P
    |proj(S0)| = 8
  end note

  :<b>counts</b>: apportion(4, 3 cells per stratum) -> 1, 1, 2
  var1 drops a dimension, so the overlap count is set PER
  STRATUM as round(0.5 * p_j), not apportioned globally:
  p_j depends on where var0 landed, which a worker holding
  one chunk cannot see for the other strata;

  :<b>per stratum</b>, rng = stream(1, VAR, 1, j)
    j | n | p | free | ideal       | lo | hi | n_overlap
    0 | 1 | 2 |  1   | round(1.0)=1 | 0  | 1  | 1
    1 | 1 | 3 |  0   | round(1.5)=2 | 1  | 1  | 1  clipped
    2 | 2 | 3 |  0   | round(1.5)=2 | 2  | 2  | 2;
  note right #FDF1F1
    printed: "WARNING var1: overlap target not reachable
    in 1 of 3 strata (e.g. wanted 2 of 3 reference cells,
    used 1; 0 cells free of var0)."
    Stratum 1 has one var1 cell to place, so it
    cannot put 2 on var0's projection.
  end note

  :var1 cells, drawn from proj_j(S0)
  (x0,x1) = (0,0), (1,1), (2,0), (2,1), each at x2 = 1;
  note right
    var1 placed in the full grid
    (0 = var0 only, B = both, 1 = var1 only)
           x0=0         x0=1         x0=2
           x2: 0 1 2    x2: 0 1 2    x2: 0 1 2
      x1=0     . B 0        0 0 .        . B .
      x1=1     . . .        . 1 0        0 1 .
      x1=2     0 0 .        . . 0        . 0 0
    (1,1,1) and (2,1,1) share no SITE with var0, yet they
    count as overlap: var0 holds (1,1,2) and (2,1,0),
    which project onto the same (x0, x1) cells.
  end note

  :<b>OverlapCalculator.compute_overlap_report</b>
  overlap   = 4 shared / 8 cells of proj(S0) = <b>0.500</b>
  overlap_r = 4 shared / 4 cells of var1     = <b>1.000</b>;
  note right
    The per-stratum rounding happens to sum to the
    goal here (1 + 1 + 2 = round(0.5 * 8) = 4). In
    general it drifts by order sqrt(num_strata)/2.
  end note
}

partition "two in-memory stores" {
  :<b>NetCDFBuilder.build_dataset</b>
  var0 (x0, x1, x2) 3x3x3
  var1 (x0, x1) 3x3: squeeze_constant_dims drops x2
  attrs: var_num_obs=[12, 4], overlap_target=[0.5],
  overlap_actual=[0.5], overlap_actual_reverse=[1.0];

  :<b>ParquetBuilder.build_multi_var_dataframe</b>
  one row per (x0, x1, x2) held by either variable:
  12 var0 sites + 2 var1-only sites = 14 rows
  var1's rows carry x2 = 0.139544, its pinned label;
  note right
    DatasetDescription of the written file:
    |= var |= dims |= var_sites |= occupied |= overlap |= overlap_reverse |= unused_coords |
    | var0 | (x0, x1, x2) | 27 | 12 | NaN | NaN | 0 |
    | var1 | (x0, x1) | 9 | 4 | 0.5 | 1.0 | 1 |
    var1 never uses x1 = 2: one unused coordinate.
  end note
}

partition "disk" {
  :netCDF/ds.nc                13681 B
  parquet/ddf_0.parquet         4510 B
  parquet/_metadata             3765 B
  parquet/_common_metadata      3025 B;
}

:return (Dataset, DataFrame);
stop

@enduml
